.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yume
is the native YUME Transport Protocol 1 client.
It reads a schema-1 client configuration, maintains an authenticated
session to
.BR yumed (8),
and runs the configured SOCKS5 and forward listeners.
SOCKS5 CONNECT carries TCP streams; UDP ASSOCIATE carries datagrams
through a configured packet service.
A forward turns each connection to its loopback port or UNIX socket into
a stream on its service, optionally to a fixed destination.
The server enforces each service's destination policy.
.PP
A Linux packet adapter connects a named service to a managed IP/TUN
interface and owns its addresses, routes and optional per-link DNS.
The client is not yet qualified for production.
Check
.B docs/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md
before deployment.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--config " path
Read exactly one schema-1 JSON configuration.
Its role must match the program: client for
.BR yume ,
server for
.BR yumed .
Required unless
.B --help
or
.B --version
is requested.
Security policy has no command-line overrides.
.TP
.B --validate
Check schema, role, referenced credentials, direct-adapter destination
policy and the daemon's module programs, then exit without opening a
listener or network connection.
This checks local inputs; it does not test connectivity or complete
runtime startup, including loading the cover site, matching services to
runtime adapters, TUN privileges or DNS authorization.
.TP
.B --version
Print the product version, transport version, configuration schema,
suite, session-security provider, crypto backend and evidence profile.
This operation uses local information and does not read a configuration
or contact a server.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print the supported options and exit.
Unknown arguments still fail parsing when combined with
.B --help
or
.BR --version .
.PP
Each run setting replaces one configuration key for this run only and
passes the same checks as the file's value.
An error names the key's JSON pointer and says that the value came from
the command line.
No run setting can change the wire image, authentication, encryption,
admission, destination policy or leak protection.
.B --validate
prints every key a run setting can replace, with its value and whether
it came from the configuration or a flag.
.TP
.BI "--connect " ip
Dial this IP literal instead of resolving the configured host, as
.B endpoint.connect_address
does.
The TLS server name stays the configured host, and TLS and admission
still authenticate it.
Through a configured SOCKS5 upstream proxy, the proxy connects to this
address.
.TP
.BI "--socks-address " ip
Set the listen address of the configuration's only SOCKS5 adapter.
The configuration's rule applies: 127.0.0.1 or ::1.
.TP
.BI "--socks-port " port
Set the listen port of the configuration's only SOCKS5 adapter, 1 to
65535.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration owns endpoint addresses, exact suite, credential file
references, cover profile, services, adapters and resource limits.
The schema rejects unknown fields, wrong types and unsupported values.
Credential paths are relative to the configuration file's directory
unless absolute.
Credential loading rejects unsafe file types and permissions; inline
secrets are forbidden.
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGINT
and
.B SIGTERM
request shutdown of listeners and sessions, followed by removal of owned
TUN networking.
.B SIGPIPE
is ignored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates successful help, version or validation output, or
shutdown requested by a handled signal with successful cleanup.
Exit status 1 indicates a runtime or internal failure.
Exit status 2 indicates invalid arguments, configuration or startup
prerequisites.
Diagnostics go to standard error; help and version output go to standard
output.
Argument errors also print usage on standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate an existing client kit, then start its configured listeners:
.PP
.nf
yume --config /path/to/client.json --validate
yume --config /path/to/client.json
.fi
.PP
The separately installed
.B yume-setup
and
.B yume-doctor
tools provision and inspect schema-1 kits.
Their
.B --help
output describes their arguments.
Setup and doctor are separate programs.
